 ## 英文正式图注
 
-**FIG. 4.** Resolved transport coefficients of the rectangular groove array at $P=240$ nm, $w=120$ nm. (a) Along-groove $K_\parallel$ (filled symbols, solid lines) and across-groove $K_\perp$ (open symbols, dashed lines) against groove depth $d$, at four residual gaps. (b) Anisotropy ratio $A=K_\parallel/K_\perp$ on a logarithmic ordinate; the dotted line marks $A=1$. Coefficients are given per unit width, in m³; division by the equivalent-volume height $H_{\rm ref}=h+\varphi d$ gives the three-dimensional permeability in m², consistent with the volume-averaged velocity $\bar u=J/H_{\rm ref}$ defined in Sec. II. Within the sampled depth range the $K_\perp$ curves in (a) are nearly horizontal: at fixed gap $K_\perp$ varies by at most 3.7% over the sampled depths (largest at $h=25$ nm, where the sampled depths are only $d=25$, $50$ and $100$ nm). The depth is the abscissa because it is the variable that the along-groove coefficient follows; the gap is the variable that the across-groove coefficient follows, and it enters only through the series label. The matrix is not a full rectangle: at $h=25$ nm only $d\le100$ nm was computed.
